@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Privacy policy for Swords and Ravens, the free online Game of Thrones: The Board Game platform.";
}
<div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 [&_h2]:text-secondary [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:mt-6 [&_p]:text-base-content/80">
<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary mb-2">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    This page summarizes what account and cookie data Swords and Ravens stores
    about you, and how you can request it be removed.
</p>

<h2>Account data</h2>
<p>
    When you register, or sign in via Google, Discord, or Facebook, we store your username,
    e-mail address (if provided by the sign-in method), and gameplay-related settings and
    statistics (game history, win rate). If you sign in with an external provider, we never see or
    store your password on that provider — only the profile fields it explicitly shares with us.
</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>
    We use a session/authentication cookie to keep you signed in; this cookie is essential and is
    set as soon as you sign in, independent of the consent banner. We do not use analytics or
    advertising cookies of our own. If you sign in via an external OAuth provider, that provider
    may set its own cookies during the redirect — see their respective privacy policies.
</p>

<h2>Security and availability</h2>
<p>
    To protect the site from excessive requests, we temporarily use your account identifier or IP
    address to enforce request limits. These limits are held in the website's memory and reset when
    it restarts.
</p>
<p>
    To monitor availability and performance, we retain aggregated request counts, response times,
    and website process resource measurements for up to seven days. These aggregates do not contain
    account identifiers, IP addresses, individual URLs, or query parameters.
</p>
<p>
    To protect the site against excessive use, we also count authenticated website requests per
    account for the current UTC hour, including requests rejected by the rate limiter. Static files
    and requests denied by authorization are not counted. Administrators can view these counts.
    We rely on our legitimate interest in keeping the service available;
    the previous hour's account counts are removed shortly after the hour ends while the website is
    running. These counts do not include individual URLs or query parameters.
</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>
    You can review and update your profile settings from your account page at any time. To request
    a full export or deletion of your account data, or to object to processing based on legitimate
    interests, contact the site operator. You may also lodge a complaint with a data protection authority.
</p>
</div>
